.TH TUI_STATUSLINE_INIT 3 2026-10-14 "libtuikit 0.8" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_statusline_init, tui_statusline_free, tui_statusline_set_hints,
tui_statusline_set_help, tui_statusline_hint_count, tui_statusline_hint_at,
tui_statusline_hints_fit, tui_statusline_set_message,
tui_statusline_clear_message, tui_statusline_message, tui_statusline_set_wait,
tui_statusline_clear_wait, tui_statusline_set_position,
tui_statusline_set_position_index, tui_statusline_begin_prompt,
tui_statusline_prompt_active, tui_statusline_prompt_text,
tui_statusline_handle, tui_statusline_render, tui_statusline_format \-
the status line: key hints that fit, a message, a wait text, a position, a prompt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/statusline.h>
.PP
.BI "void tui_statusline_init(tui_statusline *" sl );
.BI "void tui_statusline_free(tui_statusline *" sl );
.BI "int  tui_statusline_set_hints(tui_statusline *" sl ", const tui_statusline_hint *" hints ", int " n );
.BI "void tui_statusline_set_help(tui_statusline *" sl ", const char *" key ", const char *" label );
.BI "int  tui_statusline_hint_count(const tui_statusline *" sl );
.BI "const tui_statusline_hint *tui_statusline_hint_at(const tui_statusline *" sl ", int " i );
.BI "int  tui_statusline_hints_fit(const tui_statusline *" sl ", int " cols );
.BI "void tui_statusline_set_message(tui_statusline *" sl ", const char *" text ", tui_style " style );
.BI "void tui_statusline_clear_message(tui_statusline *" sl );
.BI "const char *tui_statusline_message(const tui_statusline *" sl );
.BI "void tui_statusline_set_wait(tui_statusline *" sl ", const char *" text ", int " done ", int " total );
.BI "void tui_statusline_clear_wait(tui_statusline *" sl );
.BI "void tui_statusline_set_position(tui_statusline *" sl ", const char *" text );
.BI "void tui_statusline_set_position_index(tui_statusline *" sl ", int " cur ", int " total );
.BI "void tui_statusline_begin_prompt(tui_statusline *" sl ", const char *" prompt ", const char *" initial );
.BI "int  tui_statusline_prompt_active(const tui_statusline *" sl );
.BI "const char *tui_statusline_prompt_text(const tui_statusline *" sl );
.BI "tui_statusline_result tui_statusline_handle(tui_statusline *" sl ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "void tui_statusline_render(tui_statusline *" sl ", tui_canvas " c );
.BI "int  tui_statusline_format(const tui_statusline *" sl ", int " cols ", char *" out ", size_t " outsz );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tui_statusline
is the one bottom line of a program: a pure model drawn on the last row of a
canvas in reverse video, so that the terminal's own background is kept
elsewhere.
It is one line, never wrapped.
What it shows, in this order: the prompt while one is open, the message, the
waiting text, the key hints.
The position text is right-aligned and always kept; the rest is cut to make
room for it.
.PP
.BR tui_statusline_init ()
makes an empty line with the help hint "? help".
The struct must not be copied afterwards.
.BR tui_statusline_free ()
frees the prompt editor's memory.
.PP
.BR tui_statusline_set_hints ()
sets the hints of the view, an array of
.I "{ key, label, priority }"
the program keeps alive (it is not copied).
At most
.B TUI_STATUSLINE_HINTS_MAX
(64) entries; more fails with
.BR EINVAL .
The hints are shown in the given order, two blanks apart.
When they do not fit, the entry of the lowest priority is dropped whole, then
the next, never cut in the middle; of equal priority the earlier is kept.
The help hint is reserved first and stays; it is cut only when it alone does
not fit.
.BR tui_statusline_set_help ()
changes it; a NULL
.I key
turns it off.
.BR tui_statusline_hint_count ()
and
.BR tui_statusline_hint_at ()
give the full set, which is what the program's help screen lists;
.BR tui_statusline_hints_fit ()
how many of them are shown on a line of
.I cols
columns.
.PP
.BR tui_statusline_set_message ()
sets a transient message in
.I style
.RB ( TUI_STYLE_ERROR ", " TUI_STYLE_OK ", " TUI_STYLE_DEFAULT
for information).
The whole bar takes the style's colours, with reverse video added.
It replaces the hints until a key or a paste reaches
.BR tui_statusline_handle (),
or
.BR tui_statusline_clear_message ()
is called.
A long message is cut with an ellipsis at a display-width boundary, a wide
character whole; controls become spaces.
.PP
.BR tui_statusline_set_wait ()
sets a waiting text such as "Syncing INBOX ..." in
.BR TUI_STYLE_PROGRESS ,
with " done/total" after it when
.I total
is above zero.
It shows until
.BR tui_statusline_clear_wait ()
and may be set again from a loop that has no key press.
A message goes before it.
.PP
.BR tui_statusline_set_position ()
sets the right-aligned segment;
.BR tui_statusline_set_position_index ()
formats "[cur/total]" and clears it when
.I total
is below 1.
.PP
.BR tui_statusline_begin_prompt ()
opens a one-line input (a filter, a search) on the status row, with the given
prompt text and initial text.
While it is open
.BR tui_statusline_handle ()
gives it every event as
.BR tui_lineedit_handle ()
does and returns
.B TUI_STATUSLINE_ACCEPT
on Enter or
.B TUI_STATUSLINE_CANCEL
on Esc, Ctrl-C and Ctrl-D on an empty line; both return the line to the hints,
and
.BR tui_statusline_prompt_text ()
still gives the text.
Otherwise a key or a paste clears the message
.RB ( TUI_STATUSLINE_CHANGED )
and the event is the program's
.RB ( TUI_STATUSLINE_IGNORED
for the line).
A resize does not clear the message.
.PP
.BR tui_statusline_render ()
draws the line on the last row of the canvas; the layout follows from its
width, so a resize needs only the next render.
.BR tui_statusline_format ()
writes the same line as plain text for a line of
.I cols
columns, without trailing blanks, for a CLI or a test; it returns the length,
or \-1 when
.I outsz
was too small (the text is then cut at a character).
.SH RETURN VALUES
.BR tui_statusline_set_hints ()
returns 0, or \-1 with
.BR errno .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libtuikit (7),
